t> </non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIGE ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAMURA KAZUHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OJI YUKA SYNT PAPER CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIGE, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAMURA, KAZUHISA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OJI-YUKA SYNTHETIC PAPER CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIGE ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAMURA KAZUHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIGE, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAMURA, KAZUHISA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A multilayered stretched resin film characterized by comprising (A) a base layer comprising 40 to 90 wt.% polyolefin resin and 10 to 60 wt.% fine inorganic particles or organic filler and, formed on at least one side thereof, (B) a layer comprising 0 to 85 wt.% polyolefin resin and 15 to 100 wt.% noncrystalline resin, wherein the layer (B) has a void content of 5% or lower.  When printed by offset printing, the film can be effectively prevented from becoming wavy or curling due to the vehicle contained in the offset ink.  Thus, it has exceedingly high printability.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un film multicouche en résine étirée caractérisé en ce qu'il comprend (A) une couche de base comprenant de 40 à 90 % en poids d'une résine polyoléfinique et de 10 à 60 % en poids de fine particules organiques ou d'une charge organique et, sur au moins un de ses côtés, (B) une couche comprenant de 0 à 85 % en poids d'une résine polyoléfinique et de 15 à 100 % en poids d'une résine non cristalline, cette couche (B) ayant une teneur en vide maxi de 5 %. En impression offset, il est possible d'empêcher ce film d'onduler grâce au vecteur contenu dans l'encre d'impression utilisé pour ce procédé. Ce film se prête donc remarquablement bien à l'impression.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>